--- Step 2: GREEN — _build_v2_document semantics -----------------------------
BEFORE (mixed Task 6 interception + leftover Task-5-incompatible generation):
  | v1 input                          | result                                     |
  | empty credentials + empty targets | empty v2 doc (version 2, {}, {})           |
  | any mysql credential              | MIGRATION_REQUIRES_MANUAL_REVIEW           |
  | any mysql target                  | MIGRATION_REQUIRES_MANUAL_REVIEW           |
  | any non-empty credentials         | MIGRATION_REQUIRES_MANUAL_REVIEW           |
  | any ssh_config target             | builds ssh_config v2 -> from_mapping fails |
  |                                   | -> ConfigError -> MIGRATION_V2_INVALID     |
AFTER (this knife; L414-431 target loop replaced by a single emptiness guard):
  | v1 input                          | result                                     |
  | empty credentials + empty targets | empty v2 doc {"version":2,"credentials":{},"bindings":{}} |
  | any non-empty credentials         | MIGRATION_REQUIRES_MANUAL_REVIEW           |
  | any non-empty targets (mysql OR   | MIGRATION_REQUIRES_MANUAL_REVIEW           |
  |   ssh_config)                     |                                            |
No ssh_config v2 credential/binding is generated anywhere any more.
The explicit mysql credential/target checks (L401-408) are retained ahead of the
generic emptiness guards so the Task 6 intent stays readable.
Call order untouched: L958-959 _validate_v1_credentials/_validate_v1_targets run
FIRST (MIGRATION_SOURCE_SCHEMA), L964 _build_v2_document runs after
(MIGRATION_REQUIRES_MANUAL_REVIEW). L966-967 `except MigrationError: raise`
passes the code through verbatim; L968-973 ConfigError -> MIGRATION_V2_INVALID
fallback is UNCHANGED and still present.

