*** A2 COVERAGE GAPS (do not overstate equivalence) ***
G1. Installed-manifest-vs-live-registry agreement is no longer verified by ANY test.
    test_plugin_registration.py and test_r5_approval_host_posture.py::
    test_r5_approval_host_exactly_two_tools_posture pin the live registry to exactly two
    tools, but neither reads the INSTALLED plugin.yaml of a deployed plugin tree and compares
    it to what PluginManager actually registered. A manifest/registry divergence introduced in
    the install path would now go undetected.
G2. Replay-closed is no longer verified end to end against a manifest-consistent install.
    The behavioural replay assertions still run, so same-turn replay closure itself is still
    covered; what is lost is that it was previously asserted on a wire whose installed
    manifest was proven to match the registry. R2 one-shot consumption and the R4 result
    guard are ADJACENT, NOT EQUIVALENT: neither drives a real AIAgent replay turn.
G3. No test now executes ANY wire carrier end to end as a CLI against the live workspace.
    test_r5_wire_e2e.py::test_r5_wire_carrier_exists_and_is_not_r3_copy only proves a
    separate R5 carrier file exists and is not a copy of the R3 one — it does not run it.
    scripts/run_r5_wire_e2e.py has only run_smoke coverage
    (test_r5_wire_smoke_zero_secrets), not the nine-scenario matrix.
G4. The R3 four-tool wire itself can no longer be re-executed at all; the frozen carrier is
    now exercised only for source/AST facts plus the fixture-driven scenarios that do not
    touch the registry set. R3 remains signed off on its frozen evidence, but it is no longer
    continuously re-provable against the live tree.
All four gaps are pending the R5 wire main-chain matrix, honestly marked by
tests/test_r5_wire_e2e.py::test_r5_wire_full_main_chain_placeholder (assert False, permanent
strict xfail, deliberately retained).

